{"id": "EUVD-2026-103765", "enisaUuid": "5a4bf46c-a245-3628-b92a-35fe7e737fda", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nrtc: mpfs: fix unchecked devm_clk_get() error pointer in probe()\n\ndevm_clk_get(&pdev->dev, \"rtcref\")'s return value was passed straight\ninto clk_get_rate() without checking it for an error first, unlike the\n\"rtc\" clock a few lines above which is correctly checked with\nIS_ERR(). clk_get_rate() only guards against a NULL clk, not an error\npointer:\n\n\tif (!clk)\n\t\treturn 0;\n\t...\n\trate = clk_core_get_rate_recalc(clk->core);\n\nso if devm_clk_get() ever returns an error pointer here (for example\nERR_PTR(-EPROBE_DEFER), which is the normal, expected outcome if the\nclkcfg clock-provider this RTC depends on has not registered its\nclocks yet by the time this driver probes), clk_get_rate() dereferences\nthat error pointer instead of returning 0, crashing instead of letting\nprobe defer.\n\nCapture the clock in the existing 'clk' local and check it with\nIS_ERR() before calling clk_get_rate(), matching the handling already\nused for the \"rtc\" clock in this same function.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:49:17", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:57:15", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ab741d1b714b4acc605f3d14cdc4120f87341ed1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/74dc7c52946e3d47c40edd0875adb7cc15937066", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cfd70c9b19846c524f2b6195a7484bdf22071ccf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8a03f8422fa08eed335c51bccb612a3d81739ff2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac41b05d15db3134e839148290d67415ee0bdb58"], "aliases": ["GHSA-44qj-hfjm-pr88", "CVE-2026-98825"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0db491f9-086d-384b-a7b1-17ca088b8f3e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "1137b4eb-231a-3d74-bef9-2fb7c87866a2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.0"}, {"id": "2c8df225-3b0d-367c-9b4a-8b721fda4bb9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0b31d703598dc1993867597bbd45e87d824fc427 <74dc7c52946e3d47c40edd0875adb7cc15937066"}, {"id": "509cab97-9c7f-38bb-9d49-ed40372e0f23", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0b31d703598dc1993867597bbd45e87d824fc427 <ab741d1b714b4acc605f3d14cdc4120f87341ed1"}, {"id": "6a552049-44fa-34e4-bc09-68a85cafff64", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0b31d703598dc1993867597bbd45e87d824fc427 <ac41b05d15db3134e839148290d67415ee0bdb58"}, {"id": "6c905923-d563-3a79-80d2-eef4b67ef55b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "72c7efaa-f619-3a65-9a4e-288fe1bc9468", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "8a9f1b0d-410b-3b40-99e0-80a0b4c0bb40", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "8cbdff3e-1ddc-3cfd-b1b9-cb48fbbd611d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0b31d703598dc1993867597bbd45e87d824fc427 <8a03f8422fa08eed335c51bccb612a3d81739ff2"}, {"id": "c4889318-d143-347b-8803-c5cd4df5f6fd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "db2b1720-a65b-376b-9540-612a6d993c76", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "f1acf989-3bca-3b56-b2a7-039503c789ef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0b31d703598dc1993867597bbd45e87d824fc427 <cfd70c9b19846c524f2b6195a7484bdf22071ccf"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3bf770ce-ac81-351a-831d-1654754975ca", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}